; Two sequences compare pair by pair, and not lexicographically:
; (a, b) < (c, d) holds only when a < c and b < d, and the left sequence
; is no longer than the right.  A sequence and a number compare element
; by element: the sequence is below the number when every element is,
; and above it when every element is.
;
; A value expression evaluates `a > b` as `b < a`, so each element
; compares with `<`.

test eval '(1, 2) < (1, 3)'
0
end test

test eval '(1, 2) < (2, 3)'
1
end test

test eval '(2, 3) > (1, 5)'
0
end test

test eval '(1, 2) < (2, 3, 4)'
1
end test

test eval '(1, 2) < 3'
1
end test

test eval '3 < (1, 5)'
0
end test

test eval '0 < (1, 2)'
1
end test
